  "provenance_note": "New dated baseline after the sleep-related-coverage-loss fix. A performance review found 3 of the last 4 trading days with real, lost cycle coverage (58/72, 60/72, 1/72 scheduled slots), traced via Windows Event Log to the machine being put to sleep at night via the Start Menu Sleep button on the operator account - not a bug, not malware. Tier 1 remains byte-identical. Tier-2 changes: live_slc/run_slc_live.py - run_preflight() is now instrumented with the same _start_cycle_run(\"preflight\")/_finish_cycle_run(...) bracketing run_cycle()/run_closeout_stage() already had, so a missed or failed preflight is now visible in SlcCycleRun telemetry (previously zero telemetry existed for this stage at all). live_slc/check_schedule_health.py (new) - time-aware, structurally-read-only (sqlite mode=ro) diagnostic run by its own Scheduled Task each morning; reports preflight timing (NO_TELEMETRY_LEGACY before 2026-08-31, WARNING after), cycle-slot coverage (windows_scheduled_slots vs entry_eligible_slots, correctly narrowed on early-close days via the same entry-cutoff rule as confirmation_within_entry_cutoff()), and closeout completion; exits nonzero only on a genuine WARNING. scripts/slc_live/run_slc_schedule_health.bat (new) - wrapper for the above. scripts/slc_live/run_slc_preflight.bat, run_slc_cycle.bat, run_slc_closeout.bat - fixed exit-code masking: each wrapper previously ran an unconditional echo after its Python call with no exit-code capture, so run_hidden.vbs (Tier-2, unchanged) always forwarded success (0) to Task Scheduler regardless of the real result; each now captures %ERRORLEVEL% immediately after the Python call and ends with exit /b %rc%. live_slc/guardrails.py itself also changed (not visible in its own tier2 hash set, by the same self-reference limitation documented in its own source): GUARDRAILS_TIER2 now includes live_slc/check_schedule_health.py and scripts/slc_live/run_slc_schedule_health.bat, since that script is invoked automatically by its own Scheduled Task (the human-judgment exemption that applies to check_readiness.py/check_session_gate.py/check_paper_session_audit.py does not apply here); DEPLOYMENT_BASELINE and EXPECTED_DEPLOYMENT_BASELINE_SHA256 now point at this file. No frozen signal, market-structure, zone, stochastic, entry, stop, target, ranking, sizing, or numeric risk rule changed. See the approved sleep-fix plan for full context.",
